WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.362
Z T F Orchestrator is a web based operations console for planning,

00:00:04.788 --> 00:00:07.825
executing and tracking Nutanix infrastructure automation.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:12.450
It brings saved configuration files, secure credential references,

00:00:12.738 --> 00:00:17.612
workflows, scripts and sequential pipelines into one operator interface.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.538
Its core use is deploying A H V H C I clusters,

00:00:22.812 --> 00:00:26.538
applying their post deployment configuration, and preparing repeatable

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:27.838
infrastructure rebuilds.

00:00:28.225 --> 00:00:32.487
It helps turn a reviewed design into a traceable sequence of actions.

00:00:33.696 --> 00:00:35.808
The console is the operator entry point.

00:00:36.196 --> 00:00:40.321
A saved Y A M L file describes the intended targets and

00:00:40.333 --> 00:00:40.971
settings.

00:00:41.371 --> 00:00:45.458
Credential references identify separately stored secrets.

00:00:45.858 --> 00:00:50.196
A workflow or script selects the action to perform, and the installed

00:00:50.321 --> 00:00:53.896
execution runtime carries it out against the relevant service.

00:00:54.296 --> 00:00:59.533
The Z T F one point X runtime supports the established ZeroTouch

00:00:59.546 --> 00:01:00.671
Framework paths.

00:01:01.096 --> 00:01:05.746
The Foundation V M workflow uses its dedicated integration to submit

00:01:06.146 --> 00:01:08.408
and monitor Foundation imaging requests.

00:01:08.808 --> 00:01:13.183
The appliance runs the application and stores operational records.

00:01:14.429 --> 00:01:18.692
For a new cluster, an operator selects the correct Foundation service,

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:22.717
installation images, physical nodes and network settings.

00:01:23.129 --> 00:01:27.154
Orchestrator validates the available inputs, applies the required

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:30.454
approval controls and submits the reviewed request.

00:01:30.929 --> 00:01:34.504
Foundation performs node imaging and cluster creation.

00:01:34.904 --> 00:01:38.654
After deployment, post configuration can apply supported password,

00:01:39.104 --> 00:01:45.267
EULA, Pulse, D N S, N T P, networking and storage settings.

00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:49.529
A pipeline pairs each action with a saved file and executes the

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:50.417
steps in order.

00:01:50.817 --> 00:01:53.217
A failed step stops the remaining sequence.

00:01:54.392 --> 00:01:58.992
Disaster Recovery groups saved cluster recovery profiles by datacenter.

00:01:59.392 --> 00:02:03.942
Each profile can link the Foundation V M configuration and the post

00:02:03.942 --> 00:02:06.829
deployment pipeline needed to reconstruct that cluster.

00:02:07.229 --> 00:02:11.792
Reviewed snapshots, destructive approvals, job tracking, bootstrap

00:02:11.792 --> 00:02:15.404
configuration and health verification structure the recovery process.

00:02:15.804 --> 00:02:19.579
Re-foundation can erase existing node installations.

00:02:19.992 --> 00:02:23.367
This feature prepares the infrastructure onto which you recover.

00:02:23.767 --> 00:02:27.954
Restoring virtual machines, application data and business services

00:02:27.967 --> 00:02:31.317
remains with your backup platform and recovery procedures.

00:02:32.517 --> 00:02:37.799
Overview now brings managed cluster records open review items running jobs

00:02:37.892 --> 00:02:43.362
and fresh P E Good readbacks together Managed records link saved files

00:02:43.442 --> 00:02:48.679
pipelines and recovery profiles adding a record does not discover or deploy

00:02:48.679 --> 00:02:53.762
a cluster Collect P E health explicitly to read expected identity

00:02:53.992 --> 00:02:58.712
complete membership and reported health through verified H T T P S

00:02:59.204 --> 00:03:04.017
Evidence becomes stale after fifteen minutes A successful job or a refreshed

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:09.429
page cannot replace a fresh target readback Persistent review items retain

00:03:09.429 --> 00:03:13.792
observed failures until an operator reviews and resolves them Drift

00:03:13.792 --> 00:03:18.242
Detection and Upgrade Advisor remain separate tools for configuration

00:03:18.242 --> 00:03:22.967
comparisons and upgrade planning Neither a clean dashboard nor a saved

00:03:22.967 --> 00:03:25.912
assessment establishes recovery acceptance

00:03:26.254 --> 00:03:29.891
The established deployment and post configuration paths have been

00:03:29.891 --> 00:03:31.829
used for production cluster delivery.

00:03:32.241 --> 00:03:36.466
That experience does not make every integration equally mature or

00:03:36.479 --> 00:03:39.304
replace vendor support and compatibility checks.

00:03:39.666 --> 00:03:43.729
N K P and Z T F two point X features are

00:03:43.741 --> 00:03:47.891
explicitly labelled previews and have narrower execution boundaries.

00:03:48.291 --> 00:03:53.766
Begin at Start Here, choose deploy, configure, monitor or saved automation,

00:03:54.179 --> 00:03:56.054
and follow the relevant guide in this series.

00:03:56.466 --> 00:04:01.279
These videos use simulated console examples and synthetic narration.

00:04:01.691 --> 00:04:06.354
They demonstrate the interface without executing changes on live infrastructure.
